.Dd October 25, 2026
.Dt SYSCONF-PKG 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm "sysconf pkg"
.Nd read and modify pkg.conf and repository files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm sysconf
.Cm pkg
.Op Fl ceFinNqvx
.Op Fl j Ar jail | Fl R Ar dir
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Ar name Ns Op Ns = Ns Ar value
.Ar ...
.Nm sysconf
.Cm pkg
.Op Fl eFnNqvV
.Op Fl j Ar jail | Fl R Ar dir
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Fl a
.Nm sysconf
.Cm pkg
.Op Fl E
.Op Fl j Ar jail | Fl R Ar dir
.Fl l | L
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Cm pkg
target of
.Xr sysconf 8
is the
.Cm ucl
target
.Pq see Xr sysconf-ucl 8
with the collection of files
.Xr pkg 8
reads by default.
The syntax, the typing of values, and the rewrite are those of
.Xr libucl 3 ,
the library
.Xr pkg 8
itself links;
this target adds only the paths and the rules below.
.Pp
.Xr pkg 8
has no setter of its own for these files:
.Xr pkg-config 8
prints one merged value without saying which file supplied it, and
.Xr pkg-repositories 8
records an enable or disable override under the package database
rather than editing a repository file.
That override is
.Xr pkg 8 Ns 's
and is never written here.
.Pp
Files are consulted in this order:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
.Pa /etc/pkg/*.conf
.It
.Pa /usr/local/etc/pkg.conf
.It
.Pa /usr/local/etc/pkg/repos/*.conf
.El
.Pp
A later assignment of the same key wins.
A repository file is a set of repository tags, which is
.Xr pkg.conf 5
language for a top-level group:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
FreeBSD-ports: {
  url: "pkg+https://pkg.FreeBSD.org/${ABI}/latest",
  enabled: yes
}
.Ed
.Pp
The tag is the object name.
Address the inner key as
.Ql FreeBSD-ports.enabled
.Pq and Ql FreeBSD-ports.url , and so on .
Global options in
.Pa pkg.conf
have no dot
.Pq Ql PKG_ENABLE_PLUGINS .
Booleans read back as
.Ql true
or
.Ql false
whatever spelling the file used, and are written in the spelling the
file already uses;
.Ql ${ABI}
is not expanded.
.Pp
Files under
.Pa /etc/pkg
are the base repository definitions shipped with the system.
They are read, and
.Fl F
names them, but they are not modified.
A write of a repository key whose current value comes from one of those
files goes to
.Pa /usr/local/etc/pkg/repos/FreeBSD.conf
instead, which is what the comment in
.Pa /etc/pkg/FreeBSD.conf
asks for;
the file is created if need be.
A key already set in a file under
.Pa /usr/local/etc/pkg/repos
is rewritten in that file.
A new global key is written to
.Pa /usr/local/etc/pkg.conf .
Removing a key deletes it from the local files only;
a definition that exists solely under
.Pa /etc/pkg
is left in place and the removal reports it as unknown.
A write changes only the statement concerned, in the file's own style;
a repository override file created here takes the style of the base
file it overrides, so the two read alike.
See
.Xr sysconf-ucl 8 .
.Pp
.Ev REPOS_DIR
is not chased.
The directories above are the ones
.Xr pkg 8
uses when that list is left at its default.
Shared options are in
.Xr sysconf 8 .
Cross-file write rules are in
.Xr sysconf-targets 8 .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/etc/pkg/repos/FreeBSD.conf" -compact
.It Pa /etc/pkg/*.conf
Base repository definitions.
Read-only to
.Nm .
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/pkg.conf
Global
.Xr pkg 8
options.
Default write path for a key with no dot.
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/pkg/repos/*.conf
Local repository overrides.
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/pkg/repos/FreeBSD.conf
Default write path for a repository key.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Read and disable the ports repository without editing the base file:
.Pp
.Dl sysconf pkg FreeBSD-ports.enabled
.Dl sysconf pkg FreeBSD-ports.enabled=no
.Pp
The second command adds
.Bd -literal -offset indent
FreeBSD-ports: {
  enabled: no
}
.Ed
.Pp
to
.Pa /usr/local/etc/pkg/repos/FreeBSD.conf
when that tag is not already overridden there;
.Pa /etc/pkg/FreeBSD.conf
is untouched.
.Pp
Show which file supplies the repository URL:
.Pp
.Dl sysconf pkg -F FreeBSD-ports.url
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libucl 3 ,
.Xr pkg.conf 5 ,
.Xr pkg 8 ,
.Xr pkg-config 8 ,
.Xr pkg-repositories 8 ,
.Xr sysconf 8 ,
.Xr sysconf-targets 8 ,
.Xr sysconf-ucl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm sysconf
utility first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
